FXLoop Licensing
================

Copyright (C) 2026 Hendrik Will

FXLoop is dual-module split-licensed so that enterprises and individual
developers can adopt it safely in commercial JavaFX projects while keeping
the core engine strongly copyleft.

Module License Breakdown
------------------------

| Component | License | License Text |
|---|---|---|
| `fxloop-server`, `fxloop-agent` (and the bundled `fxloop-server-all.jar`) | **AGPL-3.0-only** (GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only) | [LICENSE-AGPL-3.0](LICENSE-AGPL-3.0) |
| `fxloop-maven-plugin`, `fxloop-gradle-plugin`, `fxloop-dev`, `fxloop-launch`, `fxloop-protocol`, `fxloop-skills`, `sample-apps/*` (and all other repository modules/files not listed above) | **Apache-2.0** (Apache License, Version 2.0) | [LICENSE-APACHE-2.0](LICENSE-APACHE-2.0) |

Target Application & Internal Use Clarification
---------------------------------------------

Using FXLoop to develop, inspect, lint, live-reload, drive, or generate
tests for commercial or proprietary JavaFX applications is normal tool usage:

- Running `fxloop-server` (locally or in CI),
- Attaching `fxloop-agent` to a running JVM (`-javaagent` or `attach`),
- Linking `fxloop-dev` during development, or
- Using `fxloop-maven-plugin`, `fxloop-gradle-plugin`, and `fxloop-skills`

does **not** cause your JavaFX application, its stylesheets/FXML, or the
JUnit/TestFX tests generated from your sessions to become derivative works
or fall under `AGPL-3.0-only`.

By contrast, forking, modifying, redistributing, embedding, or hosting
`fxloop-server` or `fxloop-agent` (or `fxloop-server-all.jar`) as part of a
third-party developer tool, IDE plugin, agent platform, or commercial
service is governed by the terms of [LICENSE-AGPL-3.0](LICENSE-AGPL-3.0)
(or a separate commercial license from the copyright holder).

